            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "I read all 12 changed paths and found no exploitable risk caused by this candidate.",
              "The decoder hashes tool_response and drops it, so no response content reaches disk. Input is capped at 64 MiB, which is a bounded memory cost.",
              "Strings taken from tool_input go through evidenceLine, which sanitizes them to one line and clips them. The call and session ids are not sanitized, but they are written as JSON, so they cannot break the line format.",
              "The recording path runs only when the binding and the workflow are owned and open. A failed write returns a single sanitized warning line and the hook does not fail.",
              "The patch contains only the hook-side changes. The sidecar file adapter, its 0600 mode and its lock are not in this candidate, so I could not judge them."
            ]
          }
