            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 12 changed paths. The PostToolUse decoder rejects non-object input, empty input, wrong-typed fields, two objects, truncated input and input over the bound. It hashes tool_response as sent and keeps a response over the 1 MiB envelope bound. posttooluse_test.go covers each of these cases.",
              "OnToolResult returns early for non-memory tools without reading the binding, and it is silent for an unbound repository, an unreadable binding store, a closed workflow or a foreign binding. A failed write, a missing log and a missing clock each produce a single-line warning. evidence_test.go in the app package covers all of these. Evidence classifies exactly the calls the gate checks, and evidence_test.go in the projection package asserts that writes and promote are not recorded.",
              "Refactoring queryArguments and textArgument into package-level functions keeps PreToolUse behavior unchanged. The RecordID parsing handles absent keys, numbers, quoted numbers, text and booleans correctly.",
              "Not provable from this candidate: the file-backed sidecar adapter, the projection hook CLI wiring for PostToolUse, the installer entries and the status label. None of these is in the diff, and the ledger marks M7b as incomplete. Their absence is declared scope, not a regression. The decoder buffers each tool_response up to 64 MiB in memory before hashing it, so the 'streaming' wording in the ADR is loose. I rated this too minor to report as a finding."
            ]
          }
        }
